# MO2 writes its per-install metadata into the mod folder; with the repo
# junction-linked as the live mod, that lands in the repo root.
meta.ini

# Contact sheets from `tools/map-icons/build.py --preview` and `--compare`: scratch
# artifacts for eyeballing candidate glyphs, and the two styles side by side, at the
# sizes they are really drawn at. One of each per style, hence the glob. The atlas
# PNGs beside them ARE committed, as with tools/role-icons.
tools/map-icons/_preview*.png
tools/map-icons/_compare*.png

# Renders from tools/route-preview/preview.py. Every one is a scratch artifact for
# judging a look -- regenerated in seconds from the scripts and the texture builder, and
# a committed one would go stale the moment a constant moved.
tools/route-preview/*.png

# route-preview imports tools/stroke-tex/build.py for its alpha functions, which leaves
# a bytecode cache beside a file that is otherwise only ever run directly.
tools/**/__pycache__/

# Contact sheet from `tools/role-icons/build.py --preview`, the twin of the map-icons
# one above: a scratch artifact, regenerated from the SVGs beside it.
tools/role-icons/_preview.png

# Output of `tools/map-icons/extract.py`: every engine map-spot cell at native size, a
# labelled sheet per category and an index.html to review them in. Extracted from the
# game's own textures in seconds, so nothing here needs to be committed.
docs/icons/
